From 0609da12977b80687b121fc484d852f0d4c46667 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:54:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Select bounded development-chain candidates without
 activating headers

Scan the persistent work-ranked inventory through fixed exclusive cursors, preserving progress across insertion revisions and verifying a stable competitive prefix before returning separate replacement-body needs and an unvalidated body-ready recovery attempt. Keep all-ancestor clock, stable source/profile/root, invalidity, body epoch and recovery/receipt/propagation fences explicit.

Preauthorize fixed-index and fork Get bounds, account partial failed-page usage, retain only bounded pending work, and refuse aliased callback reentry before output mutation. Dispatch rechecks persisted causal invalidity, exact header binding and a bounded fork; the controller retains exact choices and recovery preparation owns final resources and contextual validation.

Focused real LevelDB selector tests pass against integrated storage3ed3c26ed (packet13e4a138e): Debug1/1 in1.20s and ASan+UBSan1/1 in1.56s. Includes work-vs-height, ties, unavailable higher branch, clock rollback/thresholds, finite insertion progress, exact resident quota, failed-page accounting, aliased reentry, J/receipt restart and explicitly mechanical persisted propagation/excluded-target fixtures. No sockets, defaults, profile adoption or chain activation; only five new selector files.
